{"data": [{"author_id": "2118825964826226688", "created_at": "2026-11-11T14:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120516904242811266"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PZXDFofS0l", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jonz2915/status/2120516904242811266/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120334521815986176", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/PZXDFofS0l"}]}, "id": "2120516904242811266", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "II’m making my own video game as a complete noob. And guess what... I’m turning it into a benchmark!\n\nYou’ve heard of SWE-Bench, Terminal-Bench and ARC-AGI. But I bet you’ve never heard of one that tests how far AI can take a total noob in game dev.\n\nWelcome to NoobBench. https://t.co/PZXDFofS0l", "url": "https://x.com/jonz2915/status/2120516904242811266"}, {"article": {"title": "CLAUDE FABLE 5.2 DEEP DIVE: BENCHMARKS, REAL REVIEWS, COSTS AND A FULL TIER LIST"}, "author_id": "1228674212220395520", "created_at": "2026-11-10T06:08:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120035966840865002"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2120…", "end": 267, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120035432155201537", "start": 244, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120035432155201537", "url": "https://t.co/LgfCHXSwdz"}]}, "id": "2120035966840865002", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1387, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Claude Fable 5.2 is #1 on four independent leaderboards: 65 on Artificial Analysis, 71.31% on Vals, 174 on Epoch. At max effort it also ranks 73rd of 73 on cost and 72nd on speed. Benchmarks, real reviews, costs and an S to C tier list inside. https://t.co/LgfCHXSwdz", "url": "https://x.com/amitmuflis/status/2120035966840865002"}, {"author_id": "2037413809904599040", "created_at": "2026-11-11T07:40:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120421292608193013"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 138, "id": "1353836358901501952", "start": 126, "username": "AnthropicAI"}, {"end": 186, "id": "4783690002", "start": 171, "username": "GoogleDeepMind"}, {"end": 226, "id": "4398626122", "start": 219, "username": "OpenAI"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/claudeai/statu…", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/claudeai/status/2119867114450268322", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/bLSmi3P3uc"}]}, "id": "2120421292608193013", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 189, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119867114450268322", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Anthropic and Google released new frontier AI models this week, 24 hours apart. On the independent Artificial Analysis index, @AnthropicAI's Claude Fable 5.2 leads at 65, @GoogleDeepMind's Gemini 4 Carbon is on 60, and @OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra, first in September, is third at 57. https://t.co/bLSmi3P3uc", "url": "https://x.com/TaprConnect/status/2120421292608193013"}, {"author_id": "1319101874532978690", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:31:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120283338640621826"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Try out Artifacts created by Claude users", "display_url": "claude.ai/artifact/22cBP…", "end": 145, "expanded_url": "https://claude.ai/artifact/22cBPJt6Aos6bYpjmB1BHw#distribution", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120283342360997888/MI18Jgkv?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120283342360997888/MI18Jgkv?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 122, "status": 200, "title": "2026 AI model releases and their evals (12 companies, ranked)", "unwound_url": "https://claude.ai/artifact/22cBPJt6Aos6bYpjmB1BHw#distribution", "url": "https://t.co/3Psnma9OOh"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/UuYw6nzTBw", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_jasonwei/status/2120283338640621826/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120279131980210177", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/UuYw6nzTBw"}]}, "id": "2120283338640621826", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 296, "impression_count": 41560, "like_count": 551, "quote_count": 21, "reply_count": 75, "retweet_count": 68}, "text": "Created a \"benchmark benchmark\": a frequency distribution of which benchmarks were reported by the frontier labs in 2026: https://t.co/3Psnma9OOh\n\nSome observations:\n- HLE, SWE-Bench Pro, DeepSWE, and Terminal-Bench saw universal adoption\n- Scale AI is behind two of those four https://t.co/UuYw6nzTBw", "url": "https://x.com/_jasonwei/status/2120283338640621826"}, {"author_id": "112778517", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:24:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120206096761831885"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 21, "start": 12, "tag": "AIAgents"}, {"end": 41, "start": 33, "tag": "ByteAsk"}, {"end": 140, "start": 131, "tag": "AICoding"}, {"end": 192, "start": 181, "tag": "OpenSource"}, {"end": 200, "start": 193, "tag": "GitHub"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/4n1rudh4/statu…", "end": 224, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/4n1rudh4/status/2120183671923912774", "start": 201, "url": "https://t.co/2fdELwhTuk"}]}, "id": "2120206096761831885", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120183671923912774", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Open-source #AIAgents for C/C++: #ByteAsk claims SOTA on Multi-SWE-bench C/C++ with 60% fewer tokens. Legacy systems code is where #AICoding could unlock the most enterprise value. #OpenSource #GitHub https://t.co/2fdELwhTuk", "url": "https://x.com/Cult_Of_Token/status/2120206096761831885"}, {"author_id": "2118783766743142400", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:59:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120290182457102581"], "id": "2120290182457102581", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Jason Wei published a benchmark benchmark: which benchmarks frontier labs actually reported in 2026. HLE, SWE-Bench Pro, DeepSWE and Terminal-Bench saw universal adoption. DeepSWE went from first release in June to all 12 labs. Terminal-Bench cycled four versions in one year.", "url": "https://x.com/aidevbird/status/2120290182457102581"}, {"author_id": "1207232957552848898", "created_at": "2026-11-10T15:55:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120183671923912774"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 20, "id": "2080912926488379392", "start": 12, "username": "ByteAsk"}], "urls": [{"description": "AI coding agent for your terminal, with C/C++ build, debug, sanitizer and profiling tools. A fork of OpenAI Codex CLI. - ByteAsk/cli", "display_url": "github.com/ByteAsk/cli", "end": 245, "expanded_url": "https://github.com/ByteAsk/cli", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120183681834946560/QCP7g8an?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120183681834946560/QCP7g8an?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 222, "status": 200, "title": "GitHub - ByteAsk/cli: AI coding agent for your terminal, with C/C++ build, debug, sanitizer and profiling tools. A fork of OpenAI Codex CLI.", "unwound_url": "https://github.com/ByteAsk/cli", "url": "https://t.co/FhvdqMcdtp"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/pGNxndCYEK", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/4n1rudh4/status/2120183671923912774/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120183196554039296", "start": 246, "url": "https://t.co/pGNxndCYEK"}]}, "id": "2120183671923912774", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 631, "impression_count": 356564, "like_count": 585, "quote_count": 41, "reply_count": 72, "retweet_count": 50}, "text": "Introducing @ByteAsk \n\nYour AI C++ engineer, and a swarm of them\n\n&gt; SOTA on multi SWE bench (C/C++)\n&gt; 60% fewer tokens wrt cc/codex\n&gt; auto debug/perf/optimize/test with native C/C++ tools\n\nFree plan. Open Source.\nhttps://t.co/FhvdqMcdtp https://t.co/pGNxndCYEK", "url": "https://x.com/4n1rudh4/status/2120183671923912774"}, {"author_id": "795995869531213825", "created_at": "2026-11-10T04:40:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120013616678121694"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 247, "start": 244, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 258, "start": 248, "tag": "Anthropic"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/F2Uz9E86EC", "end": 282, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Mr_Zain72/status/2120013616678121694/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120013614710988800", "start": 259, "url": "https://t.co/F2Uz9E86EC"}]}, "id": "2120013616678121694", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anthropic shipped Claude Fable 5.2 (Nov 9): 20% cheaper API pricing ($8/M input tokens, down from $10), up to 2.5x faster output, and big benchmark jumps — SWE-bench v2 up from 56.3% to 69.9%. Built for heavy coding, research &amp; agent work. #AI #Anthropic https://t.co/F2Uz9E86EC", "url": "https://x.com/Mr_Zain72/status/2120013616678121694"}, {"author_id": "2106436566713569281", "created_at": "2026-11-11T06:12:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120399313893527649"], "id": "2120399313893527649", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Your benchmark passes. \n\nYour training data still fails. \n\n155K agent runs were ranked by trajectory quality instead of outcome, and models trained on the cleanest slice won on SWE-Bench. \n\nThey grade the answers. They ignore the mess that produced them.", "url": "https://x.com/cdas_kelvin/status/2120399313893527649"}, {"author_id": "1724577915546079232", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:05:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120321504713875594", "2120321801045655712", "2120322112401391764"], "id": "2120322112401391764", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1938, "like_count": 34, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "can we normalize benchmarking AI on what people actually care about?\n\ni dont care about another SWE-bench score\n\ni want a model that can help me find a meaningful gift, navigate a hard decision, or understand a perspective\n\nthe human experience should be the ultimate benchmark", "url": "https://x.com/timmymckeegan/status/2120322112401391764"}, {"author_id": "2116158162197725184", "created_at": "2026-11-11T03:40:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120360877777904021"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 171, "id": "1863959670169501696", "start": 157, "username": "Kimi_Moonshot"}], "urls": [{"description": "Kimi-Dev-72B benchmarks at launch: rank on the LLMBenchmark Index, results Moonshot AI reported, independent scores and price. Updated November 10, 2026.", "display_url": "llmbenchmark.ai/launches/hf-mo…", "end": 196, "expanded_url": "https://llmbenchmark.ai/launches/hf-moonshotai-kimi-dev-72b-beac6e94", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120360886250434560/jFUvx9MI?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120360886250434560/jFUvx9MI?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 173, "status": 200, "title": "Kimi-Dev-72B Benchmarks at Launch: Results Moonshot AI Reported (November 2026)", "unwound_url": "https://llmbenchmark.ai/launches/hf-moonshotai-kimi-dev-72b-beac6e94", "url": "https://t.co/7BlDcPzpZT"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/9U5Ra7knG9", "end": 220, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/llmbenchmarkai/status/2120360877777904021/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120360875995414528", "start": 197, "url": "https://t.co/9U5Ra7knG9"}]}, "id": "2120360877777904021", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Moonshot AI released Kimi-Dev-72B. Independent boards have not scored it yet; Moonshot AI reports 1 benchmark results, including SWE-bench Verified (60.4%). @Kimi_Moonshot\n\nhttps://t.co/7BlDcPzpZT https://t.co/9U5Ra7knG9", "url": "https://x.com/llmbenchmarkai/status/2120360877777904021"}, {"author_id": "222047138", "created_at": "2026-11-10T14:07:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120156461913280883"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Elixir SWE Bench results: models, quantizations, harnesses and cases passed.", "display_url": "cinderella-man.github.io/elixir-swe-ben…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://cinderella-man.github.io/elixir-swe-bench/", "start": 256, "status": 200, "title": "Elixir SWE Bench", "unwound_url": "https://cinderella-man.github.io/elixir-swe-bench/", "url": "https://t.co/QF2m8zxuDH"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/3LFuZo4F7U", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/kamilskowron/status/2120156461913280883/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120155139671486464", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/3LFuZo4F7U"}]}, "id": "2120156461913280883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 220, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I added a second axis to the Elixir SWE bench showing clearly total peak RAM+VRAM utilized across the benchmark. Now it's visually obvious that smaller models just aren't so smart as even IQ1 quants of bigger models🤔 or this is just Qwen being Qwen\n\nLink: https://t.co/QF2m8zxuDH https://t.co/3LFuZo4F7U", "url": "https://x.com/kamilskowron/status/2120156461913280883"}, {"author_id": "1724577915546079232", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:04:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120321504713875594", "2120321801045655712", "2120322112401391764"], "id": "2120321801045655712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "can we normalize benchmarking AI on what people actually care about?\n\ni dont care about another SWE-bench score\n\ni want a model that helps me find a meaningful gift, navigate a hard decision, or understand someone's perspective\n\nthe human experience should be the ultimate", "url": "https://x.com/timmymckeegan/status/2120321801045655712"}, {"author_id": "2117252327241662464", "created_at": "2026-11-11T10:54:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120470189842313453"], "id": "2120470189842313453", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Agent benchmarks like MLE-bench and SWE-fficiency stop separating models once top runs cluster, so the field ships a harder benchmark. That resets the scale without checking the old tasks were mastered. For teams picking an agent, release cadence matters as much as the score.", "url": "https://x.com/lukasyin88/status/2120470189842313453"}, {"author_id": "63657268", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:16:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120536179233923375"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/0vzpgNw4y3", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/paradite_/status/2120536179233923375/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120535756238450688", "start": 239, "url": "https://t.co/0vzpgNw4y3"}]}, "id": "2120536179233923375", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 216, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ai labs often report different setups for the same benchmark, leading to fragmented results that can't be used for comparing models.\n\nhere are some example reportings of hle, osworld 2.1, swe-bench pro, automationbench, ale and mcp atlas. https://t.co/0vzpgNw4y3", "url": "https://x.com/paradite_/status/2120536179233923375"}, {"author_id": "1579215112854016001", "created_at": "2026-11-11T09:53:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120454886684795210"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/ySzkzMxAuW", "end": 551, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NFT_Chen/status/2120444341475012935/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120442647341154304", "start": 528, "url": "https://t.co/ySzkzMxAuW"}, {"display_url": "x.com/sonuv_dev/stat…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sonuv_dev/status/2120450583798628674", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/6Vhw6t7pj1"}]}, "id": "2120454886684795210", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1594, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120450583798628674", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "QWEN4-MAX PREVIEW FINALLY GOT THE FUCKING PELICAN TO RIDE A BICYCLE 😭\n\nafter watching Claude, Gemini and Qwen struggle with this ridiculous benchmark, someone got a pelican cycling down a coastal road\n\nthe wheels are spinning, the bird is upright, and Newton is probably rolling https://t.co/6Vhw6t7pj1", "url": "https://x.com/sonuv_dev/status/2120454886684795210"}, {"author_id": "1724577915546079232", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:03:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120321504713875594", "2120321801045655712", "2120322112401391764"], "id": "2120321504713875594", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "can we normalize benchmarking AI on what people actually care about?\n\ni dont care about another SWE-bench score\n\ni want a model that can help me find a meaningful gift for someone, navigate a hard decision, or understand someone's perspective\n\nthe human experience should be the", "url": "https://x.com/timmymckeegan/status/2120321504713875594"}, {"author_id": "1682428283135336449", "created_at": "2026-11-09T22:00:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119912929344598255"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/LVXQ3gxcAA", "end": 240, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TeksEdge/status/2119912929344598255/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119888369274724352", "start": 217, "url": "https://t.co/LVXQ3gxcAA"}, {"display_url": "x.com/arcprize/statu…", "end": 264, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arcprize/status/2119871080525373922", "start": 241, "url": "https://t.co/0nXOG1fmxm"}]}, "id": "2119912929344598255", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 866, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119871080525373922", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I'm just blown away by this. Fable 5.2 w/standard harness achieves as high as 80% on ARC-AGI-3 and nearly 100% w/harness-saving-state on a benchmark released in April of this year, which most models fail to break 5%. https://t.co/LVXQ3gxcAA https://t.co/0nXOG1fmxm", "url": "https://x.com/TeksEdge/status/2119912929344598255"}, {"author_id": "1646181144793165824", "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:25:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119904226902245432"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/arcprize/statu…", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arcprize/status/2119871080525373922", "start": 246, "url": "https://t.co/gHY5uINrR8"}]}, "id": "2119904226902245432", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 80, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119871080525373922", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Claude Fable 5.2 (81.2%) is the first model to beat Astra Max  (62.7%) with both sporting just a standard harness. Those are the only two models to surpass 60% on the ARC-AGI-3 benchmark (that rates LLMs in novel environments) in such a setting. https://t.co/gHY5uINrR8", "url": "https://x.com/ardan_michel1/status/2119904226902245432"}, {"author_id": "1825752501674717186", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:45:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120558555745153492"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/mr0TGdygbJ", "end": 299